# Commit authors, as git and GitHub display them.
#
# The fork's own commits were made with a git identity left over from the previous fork's Forgejo
# (`madebyjordan@noreply.git.magicbean.dev`). That address belongs to no one here: it is a Forgejo noreply
# placeholder, and the person it was configured for has no part in this repository. Every commit that carries it is
# this fork's own work, so it is mapped to the fork's maintainer.
#
# This changes the name and address git shows for those commits (log, shortlog, blame, and GitHub's commit list and
# contributors graph) without rewriting history: no commit SHA changes, so the published releases and the nightly tags
# that embed a SHA stay valid.
#
# Deliberately NOT mapped: `madebyjordan@users.noreply.github.com`. That is a different address, and it belongs to a
# real upstream contributor whose nine pre-fork commits (AMD FSR 4.1, credited in README.md) are theirs, not this
# fork's.

HanYolo1 <git@hanyolo.org> <madebyjordan@noreply.git.magicbean.dev>
HanYolo1 <git@hanyolo.org> <HanYolo1@users.noreply.github.com>
